ds are often stacked against the player. A combination of stealth, evasion, and a little bit of brute force are the key to success.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2392330/extras/2247143385178d7b06b5b51525e50eb8.poster.avif?t=1707344348\" ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2392330/extras/2247143385178d7b06b5b51525e50eb8.webm?t=1707344348\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2392330/extras/2247143385178d7b06b5b51525e50eb8.mp4?t=1707344348\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><br><br>Several factions vie for control over the remnants of the destroyed city and its resources. Some are friends, many are foes. But it must be remembered that the enemy of your enemy might prove useful, if only for a few moments.",
